abstract: >-
  Research record of LEBRE, an online one-step-ahead forecaster for time series
  with inputs, at a fixed cost per step. Its structural core accepts each
  structural change by an anytime-valid sequential test (e-process) of
  predictive improvement; layer M1 adds a precision expert combined by
  AdaHedge, and layer M2 starts the forecast from a declared trivial reference.
  Version v0.54 (M1 dormancy, cheap equivalence report, triggered removals) was
  promoted by a pre-registered rule on 93 reserved series, with errata 01.
  Contains the Python reference implementation, a C99 port of the core with
  simulated Cortex-M4F measurements, experiment scripts, pre-registrations,
  results, frozen versions with SHA-256 manifests and the self-contained v0.54
  specification.
keywords:
  - online forecasting
  - anytime-valid inference
  - e-process
  - online multiple testing
  - TinyML
  - reproducibility
